pothesis": "Adding explicit target radius and continuous sine/cosine target-angle features to the policy observation will improve reach reliability in the negative-angle failure sector without sacrificing the accepted lineage's outside-sector generalization or hold stability.", "index": 3, "initialization": "fresh", "kind": "training", "paired_comparisons": [{"candidate": "checkpoint-100352", "candidate_wins": 0, "discordant_episodes": 37, "episodes": 200, "exact_p_value": 1.4551915228366852e-11, "net_wins": -37, "reference": "champion", "reference_wins": 37, "success_delta_percent": -18.5}, {"candidate": "checkpoint-120832", "candidate_wins": 0, "discordant_episodes": 28, "episodes": 200, "exact_p_value": 7.450580596923828e-09, "net_wins": -28, "reference": "champion", "reference_wins": 28, "success_delta_percent": -14.0}, {"candidate": "checkpoint-100352", "candidate_wins": 1, "discordant_episodes": 11, "episodes": 200, "exact_p_value": 0.01171875, "net_wins": -9, "reference": "checkpoint-120832", "reference_wins": 10, "success_delta_percent": -4.5}], "parameter_changes": [], "reasoning": {"alternative": "The negative-angle failures may be caused by PPO stochasticity or insufficient control capacity rather than target representation; in that case the added geometry features will not improve the difficult sector, or will not improve it without harming the already strong outside-sector and hold metrics.", "contradicting_observation": "The difficult-sector success remains at or below 15/21, or any local gain is accompanied by a material decline in outside-sector success or a large increase in hold interruptions.", "evidence": [{"observation": "The accepted champion is 97.0% overall, succeeds on 179/179 targets outside the difficult sector, but only 15/21 targets in the approximately -155 to -115 degree sector; it also has only one hold interruption.", "source": "research/brief.md"}, {"observation": "The six champion failures are concentrated at -133.7, -122.1, -124.7, -138.4, -143.1 and -145.4 degrees; five never enter tolerance and the remaining episode holds for only one step, indicating a localized reach problem rather than broad hold instability.", "source": "research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-2-champion-200ep-seed1-fb234ea119ba.json"}, {"observation": "The current 11-value representation includes relative end-effector error and inverse-kinematics branch errors, but does not expose target radius or a direct continuous encoding of target angle.", "source": "robot_learning/scenario/observations.py"}, {"observation": "The current strategy explicitly rejects increasing focused-sampling pressure and calls for investigating representation or control behavior while preserving strong non-focused behavior.", "source": "research/postmortems.md"}], "expected_observation": "Uniform evaluation shows more than 15/21 successes in the negative-angle sector and overall success above the accepted 97.0%, while outside-sector success remains near 179/179 and hold interruptions remain low.", "initialization_reason": "A fresh run is needed because the new observation dimensionality and semantics are incompatible with the accepted policy weights; it also measures whether the representation changes the learning outcome rather than adapting an already trained policy.", "strategy_link": "This is the first balanced representation intervention after focused sampling caused severe generalization and hold regressions. It directly tests the strategy's representation explanation without changing target exposure, reward, or the fixed evaluation."}, "recorded_at": "2026-09-05", "requested_evaluations": [{"candidate": "checkpoint-100352", "episodes": 200, "evaluation_semantics": "9233771c95e7", "label": "experiment-3-representation-comparison", "metrics": {"episodes": 200, "evaluation_artifact": "research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-3-checkpoint-100352-200ep-seed1-9233771c95e7.json", "evaluation_semantics": "9233771c95e7", "official_benchmark": false, "schema_version": 5, "seed": 1, "success_percent": 78.5}, "seed": 1}, {"candidate": "checkpoint-120832", "episodes": 200, "evaluation_semantics": "9233771c95e7", "label": "experiment-3-representation-comparison", "metrics": {"episodes": 200, "evaluation_artifact": "research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-3-checkpoint-120832-200ep-seed1-9233771c95e7.json", "evaluation_semantics": "9233771c95e7", "official_benchmark": false, "schema_version": 5, "seed": 1, "success_percent": 83.0}, "seed": 1}, {"candidate": "champion", "episodes": 200, "evaluation_semantics": "9233771c95e7", "label": "experiment-3-representation-comparison", "metrics": {"episodes": 200, "evaluation_artifact": "research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-3-champion-200ep-seed1-9233771c95e7.json", "evaluation_semantics": "9233771c95e7", "official_benchmark": false, "schema_version": 5, "seed": 1, "success_percent": 97.0}, "seed": 1}], "schema_version": 1, "scientific_strategy": "## 90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98 / Scientific strategy\n\n**Direction:** Improve full-angle reach-and-hold reliability by addressing the\nnegative-angle failure sector identified in the first baseline, while keeping\nthe fixed evaluation and objective unchanged. Experiment 2 indicates that\nfocused training exposure alone is not a safe solution because its sector gain\ncame with large regressions elsewhere.\n\n**Lessons and limits:** Experiment 1 reached 97.0% at checkpoint-100352, with\nfive of six failures never entering tolerance and concentrated between -122\u00b0\nand -145\u00b0; this supports testing training exposure to that sector\n(`research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-1-checkpoint-100352-200ep-seed1-f1f33f3d10a8.json`).\nThe evidence is one training seed and does not establish whether the sector\nproblem is caused by sampling, policy capacity, or stochastic variation.\nExperiment 2's focused-sampling checkpoint-100352 solved all 21 sampled\nepisodes in the -155 to -115 degree sector, but succeeded on only 149 of 179\nepisodes outside it and accumulated 576 hold interruptions; checkpoint-120832\nfell to 18 of 21 in-sector and 137 of 179 outside-sector successes. The\nuniformly evaluated champion remained at 15 of 21 in-sector and 179 of 179\noutside-sector successes, for 97.0% overall versus 85.0% and 77.5% for the\nfocused checkpoints\n(`research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-2-checkpoint-100352-200ep-seed1-fb234ea119ba.json`,\n`research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-2-checkpoint-120832-200ep-seed1-fb234ea119ba.json`,\n`research/evaluations/90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98/evaluation-90890200-b313-4f38-b010-de1eaaeb3d98-experiment-2-champion-200ep-seed1-fb234ea119ba.json`).\nThis remains one fresh training seed, but the paired comparisons show a\nsubstantial and consistent overall regression rather than a marginal\nmeasurement fluctuation.\n\n**Open questions:** Whether the negative-angle failures arise from policy\nrepresentation or control behavior, and whether hold instability is a\nseparate late-training effect rather than a consequence of sector exposure.\n\n**Conditional next steps:** Do not increase the focused-sampling pressure.\nInvestigate representation or control behavior for the persistent difficult\nsector, while treating hold stability as a separate mechanism; any future\nintervention must preserve the strong non-focused behavior demonstrated by the\naccepted lineage.\n\n**Reconsider when:** A balanced intervention demonstrates a sector improvement\nwithout the material outside-sector and hold-stability regressions seen here,\nor when additional evidence shows that the apparent sector effect was\ntraining-seed variation.", "status": "ok", "task_reference_evaluations": [], "training_budget_steps": 120000, "training_parent": "fresh", "training_seed": 0, "verdict": "measured as requested; awaiting researcher analysis"}
